      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, the assessment would remain the same because linguistic precision and technical specificity are inherent markers of style rather than tied to a specific name. Even if the names were reversed, Abstract 1 consistently demonstrates the sophisticated vocabulary and nuanced framing expected from established scholars in a high-impact journal. Conversely, Abstract 2's reliance on broader assertions and simplified language suggests a draft that hasn't fully undergone the polish of an experienced academic voice. Therefore, in an editorial context, the texture of the writing itself is the primary indicator of rigour, regardless of who signed the name.",
